SUMMARY:[Civil and Environmental Engineering] CEE PhD Defense: Juliet Nwag
 wu Ume-Ezeoke\, "Integrating Physics-Based Reduced Order Modeling into Ear
 ly Stage Design"
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260821T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260821T160000
DTSTAMP:20260820T134603Z
UID:stanford_campus-localist-53674973022882-53674973022883@local-events
DESCRIPTION:Abstract:\n\nThe long-run thermal and energy performance of bu
 ildings and outdoor spaces is influenced by local wind velocity fields. Th
 ese flow fields govern whether occupants can rely on natural ventilation\,
  and whether pedestrians experience comfortable streets. Yet fluid-dynamic
 al information typically enters the architectural design process at later 
 stages\, only once geometry has been cemented. Flow fields thus serve as a
  check of design decisions\, rather than a driver. Bringing velocity data
 \n\nAges: All ages\nLast synced: 2026-08-20 06:46 PDT
LOCATION:Y2E2 Building
END:VEVENT
