DESCRIPTION:Stanford Libraries now holds an 1883 edition of a rare book\,
  Les laboureurs: poème tiré de Jocelyn\, whose pages (text and ornamen
 ts) were entirely woven on a Jacquard loom by the firm of silk merchant Jo
 seph-Alphonse Henry. This exhibition explores the cultural contexts and ma
 terial conditions of Les laboureurs’ production\, and considers parall
 els between technology-driven global change in the late nineteenth century
  and in our current day. The exhibition includes microscope images reveali
 ng the\n\nAges: All ages\nLast synced: 2026-08-20 06:46 PDT
LOCATION:Green Library\, Bing Wing
